settings-theme-behaviour-card = Behaviour
settings-theme-behaviour-card-desc = Choose whether wallpaper changes also recolour the interface and desktop integrations.
settings-theme-policy-label = Palette behaviour
settings-theme-policy-desc = Follow wallpaper recolours from each applied wallpaper. Fixed palette uses one chosen palette. Keep current colours leaves the theme alone.
settings-theme-policy-wallpaper = Follow wallpaper
settings-theme-policy-fixed = Fixed palette
settings-theme-policy-off = Keep current colours
settings-theme-driver-card = Colour source
settings-theme-driver-card-desc = Choose whether skwd-wall generates colours itself or imports colours generated by the desktop shell.
settings-theme-authority-label = Colour control
settings-theme-authority-desc = Skwd-wall runs the generator below; a desktop shell instead returns its own palette from the current image.
settings-theme-authority-caelestia = Use Caelestia
settings-theme-authority-noctalia = Use Noctalia
settings-theme-authority-dms = Use DMS
settings-theme-authority-end4 = Use end-4
settings-theme-engine-card = Colour generator
settings-theme-engine-card-desc = Choose the program skwd-wall runs after a wallpaper is applied. Only installed generators appear here.
settings-theme-engine-label = Generator
settings-theme-engine-desc = Built-in Iris needs no external program. Matugen, Wallust, Pywal, and external Iris run their own palette generation.
settings-theme-engine-iris-builtin = Iris (built in)
settings-theme-engine-matugen = Matugen
settings-theme-engine-wallust = Wallust
settings-theme-engine-pywal = Pywal
settings-theme-engine-iris-external = Iris (external)
settings-theme-engine-native-legacy = Skwd-colour (legacy)
settings-theme-engine-pywal-legacy = Skwd-Pywal (legacy)
settings-theme-engine-wallust-legacy = Skwd-Wallust (legacy)
settings-theme-appearance-card = Appearance
settings-theme-appearance-card-desc = Adjust the generated palette before it is applied to the interface.
settings-theme-scheme-label = Colour character
settings-theme-scheme-desc = Sets how strongly the seed colour spreads. Tonal spot is balanced, Vibrant and Expressive use more colour, Neutral and Monochrome less.
settings-theme-scheme-tonal-spot = Tonal spot
settings-theme-scheme-vibrant = Vibrant
settings-theme-scheme-expressive = Expressive
settings-theme-scheme-neutral = Neutral
settings-theme-scheme-monochrome = Monochrome
settings-theme-scheme-fidelity = Fidelity
settings-theme-scheme-content = Content
settings-theme-scheme-rainbow = Rainbow
settings-theme-scheme-fruit-salad = Fruit salad
settings-theme-finish-label = Finish
settings-theme-finish-desc = Natural keeps the generated colours. Pastel lightens, Muted desaturates, Vibrant saturates. Text colours stay readable.
settings-theme-finish-natural = Natural (from wallpaper)
settings-theme-finish-natural-plain = Natural
settings-theme-finish-pastel = Pastel
settings-theme-finish-muted = Muted
settings-theme-finish-vibrant = Vibrant
settings-theme-variant-label = Variant
settings-theme-variant-desc = Dark or light palette. Auto chooses from the wallpaper's measured brightness.
settings-theme-variant-dark = Dark
settings-theme-variant-light = Light
settings-theme-variant-auto = Auto (from wallpaper)
settings-theme-fixed-card = Fixed palette
settings-theme-fixed-card-desc = Always use one palette, regardless of which wallpaper is applied.
settings-theme-static-theme-label = Theme
settings-theme-static-theme-desc = Choose a built-in palette, one you saved in the designer, or Custom seeds to generate one from your own colours.
settings-theme-static-theme-yours = { $name } (yours)
settings-theme-static-theme-custom = Custom seeds
settings-theme-designer-label = Theme designer
settings-theme-designer-desc = Edit each interface colour on a colour wheel and check the result in a live preview. Saved palettes join the Theme list above.
settings-theme-designer-action = Open
settings-theme-custom-colors-label = Custom seed colours
settings-theme-custom-colors-desc = Comma-separated hex colours, for example #1e1e2e, #89b4fa. Used only with Custom seeds and expanded into a full palette.
settings-theme-matugen-card = Matugen appearance
settings-theme-matugen-card-desc = Matugen generates the palette and skwd-wall imports its interface colours.
settings-theme-matugen-scheme-desc = The Material 3 scheme used for templates and the interface palette. Smart lets Matugen choose a scheme from the image’s colourfulness. Smart requires Matugen 4.2 or newer.
settings-theme-interface-finish-label = Interface finish
settings-theme-interface-finish-desc = Optional final treatment applied to the imported interface roles. It does not rewrite Matugen's external templates.
settings-theme-color-index-label = Source colour index
settings-theme-color-index-desc = Which palette slot to use as the seed colour.
settings-theme-color-index-primary = 0 (Primary)
settings-theme-contrast-label = Contrast
settings-theme-contrast-desc = Matugen contrast. Range -1.0 to 1.0 (0 = standard).
settings-theme-wallust-card = Wallust
settings-theme-wallust-palette-label = Palette
settings-theme-wallust-palette-desc = Force a wallust palette (e.g. dark16, harddark, light16). Empty = auto by mode.
settings-theme-native-card = Skwd-colour
settings-theme-native-card-desc = The older built-in extractor, kept for existing configurations. Iris produces the current palette format.
settings-theme-external-card = External palette
settings-theme-external-card-desc-noctalia = Noctalia drives colour generation. skwd-wall imports the completed palette rather than running a second colour source.
settings-theme-external-card-desc-dms = Dank Material Shell drives colour generation. skwd-wall imports the completed palette rather than running a second colour source.
settings-theme-imported-variant-label = Imported variant
settings-theme-imported-variant-desc-noctalia = Choose which Noctalia variant skwd-wall generates and imports for the current wallpaper.
settings-theme-imported-variant-desc-dms = Choose which half of DMS's generated dark/light palette skwd-wall imports for the current wallpaper.

settings-theme-matugen-smart = Smart
settings-theme-matugen-smart-mode-desc = Auto uses Skwd’s brightness detection. Smart lets Matugen choose light or dark from the image. Smart requires Matugen 4.2 or newer.
